<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  a4kStreaming browse grid (tvOS-like). The same rules as a4k-home.xml: 1080p pixels = reference app units x2, no includes and
  no named colours, Estuary font names, every control places itself (left/top), the panel says noop at its edges (a
  container without an edge action wraps). The panel is filled from Python, not a <content> row: Kodi opens its own
  context menu on a <content> row's long-press before the window's Python sees the key.

  The panel is the plugin's own listing (lists, watchlist, recommended, a year, search results, more like this, known
  for), built in the window's process. Python swaps the listing: the listing's Next item for the next page, a list or a
  person in place, Back for the step before; a4k.loading is set while one loads. Python handles OK and the long-press.

  Six columns of 232 x 348 posters in 296 x 468 slots, captions as on home. Only the poster zooms (1.08 about its
  centre): the captions keep their place, and the zoomed poster, ring and shadow stay inside the slot, clear of the row
  above and the captions below (the 248 px posters of the reference app's 124u did not fit both in 468). The focused poster has no
  fadetime: its texture is the one the unfocused layout already holds, so it shows at once. Items
  with no a4k.type (the Next item, the user's lists) are drawn as tiles: per-item <visible> on two groups in one layout,
  because an itemlayout's condition is checked once for the whole panel, not per item (seen live: every item a tile).
-->
